--- Luke 19:27-30 (para markers) ---
[v=off nl=off para=off]
And as for those who were against me, who would not have me for their ruler, let them come here, and be put to death before me. And when he had said this, he went on in front of them, going up to Jerusalem. And it came about that when he got near Beth-phage and Bethany by the mountain which is named the Mountain of Olives, he sent two of the disciples, Saying, Go into the little town in front of you, and on going in you will see a young ass fixed with a cord, on which no man has ever been seated; let him loose and take him.
[v=off nl=off para=on]
