--- Luke 19:27-30 (para markers) ---
[v=off nl=off para=off]
And as for my enemies who didn't want me to be king over them, bring them here and kill them in front of me.’” After he'd finished telling them this story, Jesus left for Jerusalem, walking on ahead. As he approached Bethphage and Bethany on the Mount of Olives, he sent two disciples, telling them: “Go to the village farther on. As you enter it you'll find a colt tied up that no one has ever ridden. Untie it and bring it here.
[v=off nl=off para=on]
And as for my enemies who didn't want me to be king over them, bring them here and kill them in front of me.’” After he'd finished telling them this story, Jesus left for Jerusalem, walking on ahead. As he approached Bethphage and Bethany on the Mount of Olives, he sent two disciples, telling them: “Go to the village farther on. As you enter it you'll find a colt tied up that no one has ever ridden. Untie it and bring it here.
