--- Luke 19:27-30 (para markers) ---
[v=off nl=off para=off]
But these oyevim of mine, the ones refusing me the Kabbalas HaMalchus (refusing my sovereignty as king) over them, bring here and execute them before me. And having said these things, he was traveling ahead, making his aliyah leregel to Yerushalayim. And it came about as he came near to Beit-Pagey and Beit-Anyah, by the Mount of Olives, Rebbe, Melech HaMoshiach sent two of the talmidim, Saying, Go to the shtetl ahead of you, in which entering you will find an AYIR having been tied, upon which none among Bnei Adam ever sat, and having untied it, bring it here.
[v=off nl=off para=on]
